Dear Hiring Team,

It is with great pleasure that I submit my candidacy for the *Software Engineer* position with *Apple*. I bring over three years of professional software engineering experience building shared APIs, intuitive interfaces, and business-critical distributed systems, together with an MS in Computer Science from Pace University. Apple's opportunity to shape frameworks that help teams deliver exceptional customer experiences strongly matches the work I have done across platform engineering, cross-functional integration, and production quality.

At Sperse, I architected a *TypeScript* and *React* visual workflow framework that lets users create, run, and manage agentic swarms through durable, resumable Temporal execution. I also designed shared *FastAPI* and *FastMCP* frameworks that expose 160+ secure backend actions with validated contracts, access control, monitoring, and integration guidance for adoption across multiple customers. That work required the same combination of API design, intuitive interface development, authentication-aware architecture, and cross-functional collaboration central to Apple's Everywhere team. To protect production quality, I built tests, documentation, GitHub Actions CI/CD pipelines, and OpenTelemetry trace-based evaluations that flag latency, accuracy, and safety issues before deployment. I would bring that attention to detail to implementing shared framework features across Apple's diverse platforms and devices.

Previously at Qualitest, I designed and implemented a cloud-agnostic *Java* and *Spring Boot API* for uploads, downloads, deletions, and authentication through expiring signed URLs across Google Cloud Storage, S3, and MinIO. I also delivered business-critical features with AWS Step Functions and Lambda across 100K+ weekly executions, and partnered with business stakeholders on the integration and adoption of optimized PostgreSQL APIs and React interfaces. These experiences strengthened my programming fundamentals and my ability to independently learn new frameworks, document integration paths, and translate stakeholder needs into dependable APIs and interfaces.

I am especially drawn to Apple's culture of *cross-functional collaboration*, its focus on creating an *extraordinary user experience*, and its commitment to privacy and accessibility as core values. I would welcome the opportunity to help the Apple Media Services Everywhere team create powerful shared frameworks that empower teams across Apple—and millions of customers—to discover, subscribe to, and engage with Apple's services. I can be reached at #ph or #eml. Thank you for your time and consideration; I look forward to connecting.

